id: pm-7gpx34
title: "GH-1528: recover completeness and TOON mistakes on the attempted read command"
description: "Wrong-command completeness spellings and --toon currently point at other commands or lose intent. Provide a typed SDK recovery resolver consumed by CLI guidance: context --full becomes --depth full; list/search --depth full becomes --full; read --toon becomes --output-format toon. Preserve all operands, tracker selection and unrelated options; refuse ambiguous or conflicting rewrites."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,read-output,recovery
created_at: "2026-10-21T07:16:02.980Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T10:41:30.545Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T10:39:31.824Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T10:39:31.824Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: The SDK emits shell-free same-command retries for GH1528 completeness and TOON cases; retries execute successfully in isolated trackers with whitespace operands and preserve authoritative bytes; conflicting or ambiguous options receive no unsafe retry; docs explain canonical controls and explicit format selection
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Expose typed SDK retry argv for completeness and TOON mistakes; CLI guidance prioritizes semantic corrections, preserves operands and tracker selection, and declines malformed or conflicting corrections. Add successful-adapter and unresolved-command regression cases."
expected_result: "Read-option mistakes receive executable same-command corrections where unambiguous, preserve read intent and authoritative tracker bytes, and remain subject to exact full-source coverage before merge."
actual_result: "All27 linked SDK/CLI cases pass, six emitted retry scenarios execute without changing authoritative bytes, unchanged-source negative control fails, and the previously missed successful adapter branch is exercised alongside refusal. Final hosted exact coverage and static checks remain required before merge."
